ROM images in this directory are NOT covered by the license of Xpeccy+
======================================================================

Xpeccy+ itself is distributed under the MIT license (see LICENSE_eng /
LICENSE_rus in the root of the project). That license applies to the source
code and to the binaries built from it. It does NOT apply to the files in this
directory.

The files in config/roms/ are firmware images of the emulated machines. Each of
them stays under the terms of its own copyright holder. They are bundled here
only so that the emulator is usable right after unpacking, and they may be
redistributed only on those terms:

  - the images must not be sold on their own, and must not be embedded into
    hardware. Bundling them with a product is allowed as long as the charge is
    for the product, not for the images;
  - the copyright messages inside the images must not be removed or altered.
    None of the bundled images was modified in any way;
  - if you are a copyright holder of any bundled image and want it removed,
    open an issue at https://github.com/dotkoval/xpeccy-plus/issues and it will
    be dropped from the next release.

AMSTRAD.copyright holds the canonical notice for the Sinclair/Amstrad images,
copied verbatim from the Fuse emulator distribution.

PROVENANCE.md lists every file actually bundled here, where it came from and
what its status is.
